From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Oct 2026 05:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media/gtkgstsink: keep GDK's EGLDisplay alive on Wayland

gtk_gst_sink_initialize_gl() wraps only the wl_display.  The
GstGLDisplayEGL child that gst_gl_display_egl_from_gl_display() later
attaches is returned non-foreign, so when the sink (or any GstGL
decoration chain, e.g. Snapshot's shutter-sound gtk::MediaFile being
dropped) finalizes it, its finalize calls eglTerminate() on the very
EGLDisplay GDK initialized process-wide (gdk_display_prepare_gl).
The next GTK frame then cannot make its GL context current: repeated
"gdk_gl_context_make_current() failed" and a frozen viewfinder while
the camera pipeline keeps running.  Regression in 4.24.1 exposed by
9139597a74 ("gtkgstsink: release GL context on disposal"), which
stopped the context leak that used to keep the display alive.

Mark the child foreign right after wrapping, per the GStreamer API
contract on gst_gl_display_egl_set_foreign(); identical to the fix
GStreamer applied to its own Qt sinks for the same fault
(gstreamer#2824 / gstreamer!8504).  Matches the fix proposed in
GNOME/gtk#8456.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/issues/8456

--- a/gtk/media/gtkgstsink.c
+++ b/gtk/media/gtkgstsink.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 #define HAVE_GST_WAYLAND_SUPPORT
 #include <gdk/wayland/gdkwayland.h>
 #include <gst/gl/wayland/gstgldisplay_wayland.h>
+#include <gst/gl/egl/gstgldisplay_egl.h>
 #endif
 
 #ifdef GDK_WINDOWING_WIN32
@@ -891,6 +892,22 @@
 
           wayland_display = gdk_wayland_display_get_wl_display (display);
           self->gst_display = GST_GL_DISPLAY (gst_gl_display_wayland_new_with_display (wayland_display));
+
+          /* The GstGLDisplayEGL child derived from this wl_display is GDK's
+           * own EGLDisplay (Mesa returns the same handle for the same
+           * wl_display), and gst_gl_display_egl_from_gl_display() returns it
+           * non-foreign, so its finalize would eglTerminate() the display GDK
+           * is still using process-wide.  Mark it foreign; the parent display
+           * keeps it alive via its qdata reference.  Mirrors the Qt sinks'
+           * fix for the same fault (gstreamer!8504, since 1.26).
+           */
+          GstGLDisplayEGL *egl_display = gst_gl_display_egl_from_gl_display (self->gst_display);
+          if (egl_display)
+            {
+              gst_gl_display_egl_set_foreign (egl_display, TRUE);
+              gst_object_unref (egl_display);
+            }
+
           self->gst_gdk_context = gst_gl_context_new_wrapped (self->gst_display, gl_handle, platform, gl_api);
         }
       else
